G'day!  From the experience of myself and some of my friends who play NetHack
regularly on Amigas using binaries ftp'ed from linc.cis.upenn.edu it appears
that this version of NetHack differs from the Unix version I compiled myself in
a couple of ways.

***** Possible Spoilers *****

1. In the Amiga binary, the is NO wand of wishing in the Castle.  In all the
times we've got to the Castle, NEVER has there been a WoW in any of the towers.
I've got to the Castle once here at work on the Unix version, and sure enough,
there was the WoW, so I know where to look.  There NEVER was any creature
capable of eating the wand anywhere near a tower, and none of the soldiers in
the passageways were carrying it.  It would appear that the person who compiled
it removed it from the level definition file before running it through the
level generator.  OK, so a WoW is pretty powerfull, it's a bit of a bummer
getting down there expecting the WoW but not being able to find it 'cos it
wasn't there in the first place!

2. There's also supposed to be an amulet of life-saving in Vlad's tower.  It
would appear that the same thing has happened here.  Though to be fair, I've
only seen Vlad's tower once, and it may be just an anomaly.  But again, there
was nothing in the tower that could have eaten it if it was there.

Can anyone else who uses the same binaries confirm this?  I'd be interested if
this really is the case.

